{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And you shall make for it a border.</b> — that he should shut the door against desires, so that he has no opening left toward them; rather he should shut against them and set them a limit. ״וְעָשִׂיתָ זֵר זָהָב לְמִסְגַּרְתּוֹ סָבִיב״ (Exodus 25:25). For the one who shuts the door against his desire — he is a free man and a king; to the exclusion of the one who breaches his fence, who is always poor in his mind. And he used the word ״זֵר״ — if he merited, a זֵר (crown) and diadem is made for him; if he did not merit, he becomes זָר (a stranger) and alien, for ״יַעֲזֹב לַאֲחֵרִים חֵילוֹ״ (Psalms 49:11)."], :book :exodus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:23:09.413589577Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}